   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>First: congrats on 0.9! This shiny/ggvis/knitr ecosystem is really turning into something amazing!</div><div><br></div><div>Second: I might be trying to use ggvis and shiny in a way that &quot;hasn&#39;t been built yet&quot;. </div><div><br></div><div>If that&#39;s the case, a perfectly acceptable answer will be, &quot;Not yet, wait until we have built it&quot;.</div><div><br></div><div>Here are the nuggets of what I am trying to do - the full shiny app is at <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/ijlyttle/9954598/99dbf4ae1084f9cc3468cd299216ccb3f223dba0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://gist.github.com/ijlyttle/9954598/99dbf4ae1084f9cc3468cd299216ccb3f223dba0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792404133605000&amp;usg=AOvVaw24cW-Ol7cKY4MMSSKJENgi\">https://gist.github.com/ijlyttle/9954598/99dbf4ae1084f9cc3468cd299216ccb3f223dba0</a> :</div><div><br></div><div>This works interactively and in shiny:</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"width:744px\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">    ggvis<span>(</span>diamonds<span>,</span> props<span>(</span>x <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">=</span> <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">~</span>table<span>))</span> <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">+</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">      layer_histogram<span>(</span>binwidth <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">1</span><span>)</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\"><span><br></span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">This works interactively but not in shiny:</font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\"><span><br></span></div><div><pre style=\"width:744px\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">    ggvis<span>(</span>diamonds<span>,</span> </div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">          by_group<span>(</span>cut<span>),</span> </div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">          props<span>(</span>x <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">=</span> <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">~</span>table<span>,</span> fill <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">=</span> <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">~</span>cut<span>),</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">          transform_bin<span>(</span>binwidth <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">1</span><span>))</span> <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">+</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">    layer<span>(</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">      props<span>(</span>x <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">=</span> <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">~</span>xmin__<span>,</span> x2 <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">=</span> <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">~</span>xmax__<span>,</span> y <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">=</span> <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">~</span>count__<span>,</span> fillOpacity <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">:=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">0.6</span><span>),</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">      layer<span>(</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">        transform_stack<span>(),</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">        mark_rect<span>(</span>props<span>(</span>y <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">=</span> <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">~</span>ymax__<span>,</span> y2 <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">=</span> <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">~</span>ymin__<span>))</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">      <span>)</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">    <span>)</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\"><span><br></span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">I suspect this has to do with non-standard evaluation not playing well with reactivity.</font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Can you guys shed any light on this?</font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:normal;white-space:normal\">(I&#39;m guessing shiny is the place to post this, but I am happy to move it to ggvis if that&#39;s the thing to do.)</span><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Side issue: could the runGist() function take a second argument based on the revision hash of a gist, in support of reproducibility?</font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Thanks,</font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Ian</font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><br></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:16.799999237060547px\">R version 3.0.3 (2014-03-06)\r\nPlatform: x86_64-apple-darwin10.8.0 (64-bit)\r\n\r\nlocale:\r\n[1] en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8/C/en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8\r\n\r\nattached base packages:\r\n[1] stats     graphics  grDevices utils     datasets  methods   base     \r\n\r\nother attached packages:\r\n [1] ggvis_0.1.0.99      devtools_1.4.1.99   OpenStreetMap_0.3.1 rgdal_0.8-16       \r\n [5] raster_2.2-31       sp_1.