=\"font-weight:bold\">~</span>xmin__<span>,</span> x2 <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">=</span> <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">~</span>xmax__<span>,</span> y <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">=</span> <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">~</span>count__<span>,</span> fillOpacity <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">:=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">0.6</span><span>),</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">      layer<span>(</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">        transform_stack<span>(),</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">        mark_rect<span>(</span>props<span>(</span>y <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">=</span> <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">~</span>ymax__<span>,</span> y2 <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">=</span> <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">~</span>ymin__<span>))</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">      <span>)</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\">    <span>)</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace\"><span><br></span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">I suspect this has to do with non-standard evaluation not playing well with reactivity.</font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Can you guys shed any light on this?</font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:normal;white-space:normal\">(I&#39;m guessing shiny is the place to post this, but I am happy to move it to ggvis if that&#39;s the thing to do.)</span><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Side issue: could the runGist() function take a second argument based on the revision hash of a gist, in support of reproducibility?</font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Thanks,</font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Ian</font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12px;line-height:16.799999237060547px\"><br></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:16.799999237060547px\">R version 3.0.3 (2014-03-06)\r\nPlatform: x86_64-apple-darwin10.8.0 (64-bit)\r\n\r\nlocale:\r\n[1] en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8/C/en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8\r\n\r\nattached base packages:\r\n[1] stats     graphics 